problem:
Problem description
- The planning horizon is one production year with seasonal labor periods $$\mathcal{S}$$, and the farm must decide a land-and-livestock operating plan over crop types $$\mathcal{P}$$ and livestock types $$\mathcal{G}$$.
- The farm has total land availability $$L$$, total development capital $$B$$, seasonal labor availability $$H_s$$ for each $$s \in \mathcal{S}$$, and external-work earning rate $$w_s$$ for each $$s \in \mathcal{S}$$.
- For each crop $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$, the labor requirement per land unit in season $$s$$ is $$\ell_{p,s}$$, and the annual net income per land unit is $$\pi_p$$. Crop cultivation uses land and labor, but it does not require dedicated capital investment.
- For each livestock type $$g \in \mathcal{G}$$, the capital required per head is $$c_g$$, the land required per head is $$\lambda_g$$, the seasonal labor requirement per head in season $$s$$ is $$m_{g,s}$$, the annual net income per head is $$r_g$$, and the housing capacity is $$U_g$$.
- The optimization goal is to maximize total annual net income from crop production, livestock production, and any external labor performed by unused farm labor.
- The total land used by crops and livestock-related feed production must not exceed available land $$L$$.
- The total capital required to raise livestock must not exceed available development capital $$B$$.
- The seasonal labor demand created by the selected crops and livestock must be covered by the available labor in each season, and any unused labor may be assigned to outside work that earns seasonal wage income.
- The number of animals of each type must not exceed the corresponding housing capacity.
- All livestock counts and all labor-day quantities must be whole numbers; fractional labor days are not allowed.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_p$$: land area assigned to crop $$p$$.
  - $$y_g$$: number of animals raised of type $$g$$.
  - $$o_s$$: number of farm labor days in season $$s$$ assigned to outside work.
  - $$Z$$: total annual net income of the operating plan.

Input Format
{
  "sets": {
    "crops": "List of crop identifiers, ordered as the index set $$\mathcal{P}$$.",
    "livestock": "List of livestock identifiers, ordered as the index set $$\mathcal{G}$$.",
    "seasons": "List of seasonal labor periods, ordered as the index set $$\mathcal{S}$$."
  },
  "resources": {
    "land_available": "Scalar $$L$$, total available land.",
    "capital_available": "Scalar $$B$$, total available development capital."
  },
  "seasonal_data": {
    "labor_available": "Vector $$H_s$$ of size $$|\mathcal{S}|$$, available farm labor days in each season.",
    "external_wage": "Vector $$w_s$$ of size $$|\mathcal{S}|$$, external-work earning per person-day in each season."
  },
  "crop_data": {
    "seasonal_labor_per_land": "Matrix $$\ell_{p,s}$$ of shape $$|\mathcal{P}| \times |\mathcal{S}|$$, labor days required per land unit for each crop in each season.",
    "annual_net_income_per_land": "Vector $$\pi_p$$ of size $$|\mathcal{P}|$$, annual net income per land unit for each crop."
  },
  "livestock_data": {
    "investment_per_head": "Vector $$c_g$$ of size $$|\mathcal{G}|$$, capital required per head.",
    "land_per_head": "Vector $$\lambda_g$$ of size $$|\mathcal{G}|$$, land required per head.",
    "seasonal_labor_per_head": "Matrix $$m_{g,s}$$ of shape $$|\mathcal{G}| \times |\mathcal{S}|$$, labor days required per head in each season.",
    "annual_net_income_per_head": "Vector $$r_g$$ of size $$|\mathcal{G}|$$, annual net income per head.",
    "capacity": "Vector $$U_g$$ of size $$|\mathcal{G}|$$, maximum feasible head count for each livestock type."
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "plan": {
    "crop_area": "Vector $$x_p$$ of size $$|\mathcal{P}|$$, planned land area for each crop.",
    "livestock_count": "Vector $$y_g$$ of size $$|\mathcal{G}|$$, planned head count for each livestock type.",
    "external_labor_days": "Vector $$o_s$$ of size $$|\mathcal{S}|$$, planned outside-work labor days in each season."
  },
  "objective": {
    "total_annual_net_income": "Scalar $$Z$$, the maximum achievable annual net income."
  }
}

